imagery.basemap
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

**Download a satellite basemap.** Stitches Bing or Google satellite tiles over a region into one georeferenced GeoTIFF. An existing file for the same provider, zoom and bounds is reused instead of downloaded again.

*Inputs*

.. list-table::
   :header-rows: 1
   :widths: 18 10 10 62

   * - Name
     - Kind
     - Required
     - Description
   * - ``region``
     - region
     - no
     - Area to cover: a WGS84 box, or a GeoJSON file whose extent is used.

*Parameters*

.. list-table::
   :header-rows: 1
   :widths: 22 14 14 50

   * - Name
     - Type
     - Default
     - Description
   * - ``provider``
     - string
     - ``"bing"``
     - Tile provider. One of: ``"bing"``, ``"google"``.
   * - ``zoom``
     - integer
     - ``19``
     - Web Mercator zoom level (Bing up to 20, Google up to 21). One level up doubles the resolution and quadruples the tile count. Must be at least 10 and at most 21.
   * - ``max_tiles``
     - integer
     - ``2500``
     - Refuse the download when the region needs more tiles than this. Must be at least 1.
   * - ``max_workers``
     - integer
     - ``10``
     - Concurrent tile downloads. Must be at least 1.

*Outputs*

.. list-table::
   :header-rows: 1
   :widths: 22 12 66

   * - Name
     - Kind
     - Description
   * - ``raster``
     - raster
     - The stitched GeoTIFF.

data.download
~~~~~~~~~~~~~

